1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,880
Piano music plays

2
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:33,590
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:36,300
Come on, Mom, please buy me a gun.

4
00:01:36,580 --> 00:01:38,677
Well, what do you call
that thing in your hand?

5
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:40,300
I mean a real one.

6
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,324
You're not old enough, Tawness.

7
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:43,800
Yes, I am.

8
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:46,451
I'll clean out the Thomas table every day.

9
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,180
Come on, Mom, please.

10
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:51,320
I'll be careful, I promise. Please.

11
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,860
Oh, my God!

12
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:39,920
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha...

13
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:51,460
Ha, ha, ha...

14
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:58,097
Vasha Stampede, the humanoid
typhoon taken down at Inepril City.

15
00:02:58,180 --> 00:02:59,460
Nice headline.

16
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,580
The 60 billion double dollars is ours!

17
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:07,860
I'm so excited I can shit.

18
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,857
Not only are we disgustingly rich,

19
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:12,881
we're going to be famous
across the entire galaxy.

20
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,580
You're acting awfully cautious.

21
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:17,400
It's okay, he's dead.

22
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:20,555
I can't help it, it's him lying there.

23
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:25,580
Hey, cheer up, you look so depressed.

24
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:27,637
This is a great day for us.

25
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:31,617
With what we just earned, we can have
this restaurant rebuilt if you want.

26
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:32,530
Do you mean it?

27
00:03:32,613 --> 00:03:34,107
Damn straight, sweet cheeks.

28
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:37,769
Me and my esteemed partners
here are multi-billionaires now.

29
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:39,597
Oh, I'm so relieved.

30
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,445
I was very worried about that.

31
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,820
You reek of tomatoes.

32
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:46,490
I know.

33
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:49,217
When I was trying to run away,
it got dumped all over me.

34
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:52,535
Hey, would you mind reimbursing
me for my dry cleaning?

35
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:54,500
I'll reimburse you, all right.

36
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:58,140
With a one-way ticket to the pearly gates!

37
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,196
You're so impatient.

38
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,397
Hey, why do you have to be in such a rush?

39
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:10,837
Come on, let's just talk it over.

40
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:12,940
Who the heck are you, mister?

41
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:16,737
I get so embarrassed when
I have to introduce myself.

42
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:19,457
But since you were asked,
I'm like a hunter of peace.

43
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:22,011
One who chases the elusive mayfly of love.

44
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:23,909
Well, something like that.

45
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,368
Ah, kill that motherfucker!

46
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:28,662
Are you insane?

47
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:31,117
Do you want to die stupid?

48
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,217
He just shot us all!

49
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,977
Next time he might use real bullets!

50
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,577
It's okay, shoot if you want.

51
00:04:35,660 --> 00:04:36,490
Try your luck.

52
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,070
No way!

53
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:38,983
Don't provoke him!

54
00:04:39,066 --> 00:04:39,896
Don't provoke him, Mr.

55
00:04:39,979 --> 00:04:40,809
Potter!

56
00:04:40,892 --> 00:04:44,580
Give it up!

57
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:49,582
With the exception of this guy, I'm afraid
you've used up all your bullets already.

58
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:51,200
I don't understand.

59
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,617
How could you tell?

60
00:04:52,700 --> 00:04:53,560
I counted.

61
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:01,181
Gee, I really hope it's
not cold outside for them.

62
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,717
Here's your gun, partner.

63
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,800
It really helped.

64
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,136
Thank you very much.

65
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,556
That was quite impressive, young man.

66
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,180
A dangerous situation.

67
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:16,337
Have you always survived like
that without shooting anyone?

68
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:17,757
Because it's too wasteful.

69
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:19,657
After all, I can come into
a restaurant like this?

70
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,237
and order an entire stack of pancakes.

71
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:23,237
for the price of one silly bullet.

72
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,900
You are a strange one.

73
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:28,177
It seems very odd that you
consider yourself a gunman.

74
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,554
You got a point there.

75
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:37,040
I'm very sorry.

76
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,610
Huh?

77
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:42,800
I really hate to do this,
son, but you are Mr.

78
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:44,725
Vash the Stampede, aren't you?

79
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:45,890
Uh...

80
00:05:45,973 --> 00:05:46,803
I am sorry.

81
00:05:46,886 --> 00:05:48,557
Please die without the fuss, okay?

82
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:51,400
I'm sorry about this, Mr. Vash, sir.

83
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,240
Hey. No biggie.

84
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:00,937
Oh, my gosh.

85
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:02,902
Half the city is buried in sand.

86
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:06,639
Their plant probably broke
down and stopped working.

87
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:09,025
Well, then they should fix it.

88
00:06:09,460 --> 00:06:13,217
Do you have any idea how much repairs
to a plant that size can cost?

89
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:14,720
Why? Is it expensive?

90
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:21,788
This time it looks like
the rumors are true.

91
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,440
You're smiling, huh?

92
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:27,600
I am not smiling.

93
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:31,097
Now we have to go run risk
prevention and get this documented.

94
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:35,827
This time we will find the real Vash the
Stampede and bring about his downfall.

95
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,680
Can this be the end?

96
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:44,840
There he is! In here! Oh crap!

97
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,370
There we go!

98
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:50,090
That's him!

99
00:06:50,173 --> 00:06:52,820
We've got you now! Oh
really? Do you mean me?

100
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:03,700
Everyone's so busy today!

101
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,397
Mama, why does this keep happening to me?

102
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,497
I haven't done anything wrong,

103
00:07:08,580 --> 00:07:10,817
but I'm always in trouble and
everybody's always picking on me!

104
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:11,730
What do I do, Mama?

105
00:07:11,813 --> 00:07:12,643
Oh!

106
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,180
Why am I crying in French?

107
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:18,690
I see him.

108
00:07:18,773 --> 00:07:19,603
He's up there.

109
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,380
He's all mine!

110
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:25,440
Get me out of here!

111
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,230
Uh-oh.

112
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:31,057
Looks like things are getting
pretty heated up down there.

113
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:35,437
We have to do something before the entire
city and everyone in it is blown away.

114
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:39,440
But if they're this agitated, I
wonder if it really might be him.

115
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,140
Let's stop this now. Come on.

116
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,817
Hey, wait a minute, Meryl.

117
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:44,730
Come back.

118
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:46,210
Meryl!

119
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:48,830
No!

120
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:52,330
No!

121
00:07:52,413 --> 00:07:53,440
I like so bad.

122
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,100
I can't stand it!

123
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:56,850
Damn it!

124
00:07:56,933 --> 00:07:58,657
Who's that deal with
his use of the grenade?

125
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:02,497
He can't be identified for the reward
if he's a pilot car, you dumbass!

126
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:03,410
This is bad.

127
00:08:03,493 --> 00:08:04,537
People out of control.

128
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,620
Complete mayhem.

129
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,760
Attention! Excuse me!

130
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:12,977
If you'll just listen to your mind,
I'm very sorry to disturb you.

131
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:16,297
My name is Meryl Stryfe from the
Burner Daily Insurance Society,

132
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:17,615
and I'm here to stay.

133
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,677
The man you're well after,

134
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:24,257
the one who's known as Bash the
Stampede, is a very dangerous man.

135
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:26,437
In order to protect your
precious lives and all

136
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:29,217
of your valuable possessions
from any further home.

137
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,594
This is a message from Mission Control.

138
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:35,476
Temporarily suspend all
pursuits of Bash the Stampede.

139
00:08:35,740 --> 00:08:37,740
Everybody proceed to base at once.

140
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:39,540
Ugh, temporarily?

141
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,717
What the hell's the matter with them?

142
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,100
Stop all pursuit now!

143
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:47,977
Well, what are we supposed
to do now, Chairman?

144
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:51,766
The damage and casualties are
just getting worse by the moment.

145
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:56,097
I cannot believe we still haven't caught
this guy after four hours of fighting.

146
00:08:56,180 --> 00:08:57,010
Caught him?

147
00:08:57,093 --> 00:08:58,195
The guy's impossible.

148
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:01,317
He's managed to run away without
returning a single bullet.

149
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:03,000
He's just too good for us.

150
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:05,437
If we make him mad, there's no telling.

151
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:08,937
Chairman, perhaps we should stop this
while the city is still standing.

152
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:10,491
That goes without saying.

153
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,197
Where can I find the man in charge?

154
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,217
I need to speak to him.

155
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,947
And just who are you people?

156
00:09:16,220 --> 00:09:17,926
Let me see the man in charge!

157
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,257
How can you allow this to happen?

158
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:22,458
This is an outrage!

159
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:25,257
You can't possibly take
out the humanoid typhoon,

160
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:28,037
no matter how many thousands
of people you set on him.

161
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:30,617
Uh, yes, I know that
the risk is very high.

162
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:35,582
But, Miss, you must understand that we
really need that $60 billion double dollars.

163
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:38,980
It's for the plant, isn't it?

164
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,350
That's right.

165
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:45,037
Because of a support system bug, over
half of the plant is completely unusable.

166
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,600
But if you mess with Mr.

167
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,397
Vash and the entire city gets wrecked,

168
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:51,297
you're going to have a lot more
than just the plant to worry about.

169
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:52,210
Oh, no.

170
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,500
It may already be too late.

171
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:57,157
I thought we should fight fire with fire,

172
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:59,077
so that's when I called
in our last resort.

173
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:01,660
And, sir, just what is our last resort?

174
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:03,700
Hmm, that. What?

175
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:17,860
It's over.

176
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:19,460
It's all over.

177
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:26,840
Can somebody tell me who or what that is?

178
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,117
It's the Nebraska family.

179
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:31,318
All right, who's the idiot
that parked this car here?

180
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:34,757
Are you trying to make
my son trip or what?

181
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:35,797
Look, you heard him.

182
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:38,174
Move it now, you damn ignorant drivers.

183
00:10:38,460 --> 00:10:40,519
Let me borrow that thing right now.

184
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,097
Nebraska family, what are you doing here?

185
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:46,377
Both of you are supposed to be
serving a jail term of 700 years.

186
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:47,872
Shut your stinking trap.

187
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:50,797
We released ourselves yesterday
at our own discretion.

188
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,940
That, that is called a jailbreak.

189
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,320
Gee, that's too bad.

190
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,397
And I was getting quite
fond of the quiet life.

191
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,900
But then again,

192
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:03,637
who can lie idle knowing that 60 billion
double dollars is there for the taking?

193
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,420
Isn't that right, Goofchef?

194
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:10,000
The infamous Nebraska family.

195
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:14,120
Convicted felons of over
150 Class A offenses and...

196
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,557
Tell me you're not gonna stick that
big oaf on Vash the Stampede now.

197
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,287
Well, it seemed like a
good idea at the time.

198
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,077
Oh, I'm sick of this!

199
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:25,857
Why does every situation we run
into take the worst possible turn?

200
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:27,411
I can't stand it anymore!

201
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,740
We caught Sammy the Stampede! Huh?

202
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:34,480
Down here, I said we caught
Vash the Stampede! Eh?

203
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,040
Like I said before, we
caught Vash the Stampede!

204
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,580
Do you mean you really caught him?

205
00:11:57,380 --> 00:12:00,880
Well, maybe they've decided
to give up after all, huh?

206
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:05,710
Ah!

207
00:12:05,793 --> 00:12:06,623
I'm alive!

208
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:08,010
Oh?

209
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,620
Don't move, Mr. Vash!

210
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:14,120
Huh? Uh-oh.

211
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,350
Hey, Sandy!

212
00:12:16,433 --> 00:12:18,017
Go tell Control that we've caught him!

213
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:19,577
We've caught Vash the Stampede!

214
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:20,490
Tell them to hurry!

215
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:21,403
Right!

216
00:12:21,486 --> 00:12:22,420
Be quick now!

217
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,760
Bounty hunters in aprons?

218
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:30,479
Wouldn't want children to see this.

219
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:32,510
That's right.

220
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:34,584
We don't want them to see this.

221
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:36,327
But we have no other choice.

222
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,877
We desperately need money.

223
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,940
I have a son lying sick at home,

224
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:43,997
but the town doctor decided to take
off and abandon this dying city.

225
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:46,117
I don't know what's wrong with my boy.

226
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:48,380
I can't just stand back and wait.

227
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:50,277
There's no one left to help him here.

228
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:52,577
That's why, that's why I...

229
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:56,617
The people, the land, everything went
wrong after the plant malfunctioned.

230
00:12:56,700 --> 00:13:00,112
But not everyone is rich enough
to leave this damned city.

231
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:02,937
We need money to call the
engineers to fix the plant.

232
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:05,549
Unless it's repaired,
the city is finished.

233
00:13:05,680 --> 00:13:07,209
Along with everyone in it.

234
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,280
Only one person has to
die to save this city.

235
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,980
So please, Mr.

236
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,433
Vash, give yourself up.

237
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,760
Please don't move.

238
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,882
I understand your situation
better than you know.

239
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:28,120
However… No! Please, sir! Don't do that!

240
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:34,020
Until I see this man you're after,
I have no choice but to keep moving!

241
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:43,520
Now please, for the love of
God, don't shoot that gun.

242
00:13:51,460 --> 00:13:52,680
Everybody get down!

243
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,100
Over there!

244
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:02,380
Right, I see it!

245
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:06,274
Bash, the stampede is right over there!

246
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,230
Bingo!

247
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:10,560
That was so easy!

248
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:11,920
Almost too easy!

249
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,061
Are you down after only one shot?

250
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:15,440
That's funny!

251
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:16,620
That is so funny!

252
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,240
What?

253
00:14:25,360 --> 00:14:27,007
Where was Vash the Stampede?

254
00:14:31,880 --> 00:14:32,717
Huh?

255
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:33,940
What the hell?

256
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:50,620
That's him.

257
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:53,157
The Devil's Helper who single-handedly

258
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,946
reduced a city of one
million people to ashes.

259
00:14:56,320 --> 00:15:00,840
The legendary outlaw Vash the
Stampede is just over that hill.

260
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:23,757
That can't...

261
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:24,740
No way!

262
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:33,020
My, my, that's more like it.

263
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:36,357
Hey, wait a minute.

264
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,517
Isn't there something
wrong with this picture?

265
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:40,776
They must know that man can't be him.

266
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:44,757
Vash the Stampede is a horrible fiend.

267
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:47,487
If you get in his way,
he can destroy cities.

268
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:51,036
And he can get out of the
worst situations imaginable.

269
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:57,501
Even if he's up against a thousand men,
he'd find a way to emerge without a scratch.

270
00:15:59,020 --> 00:15:59,850
That...

271
00:15:59,933 --> 00:16:00,763
that's who...

272
00:16:00,846 --> 00:16:03,040
What now, Vash the Stampede?

273
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:09,840
That's him, Vash the Stampede.

274
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:14,466
What's the matter, buddy boy?

275
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:15,993
Are you chickening out?

276
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:29,560
Well, aren't you a nice guy?

277
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:38,620
Hey, time's up, Wonder Boy.

278
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:41,507
Throw the fear of death
into him, ghost chef.

279
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,557
Chairman, that damn
Nebraska's a loose cannon.

280
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:53,917
I'm sorry, I didn't
want anyone to get hurt.

281
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:55,294
How could you do that?

282
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:09,835
Ugh, I can't believe you both
are still alive and well!

283
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:14,240
I was kinda hoping you ditch the
woman and save your own skin!

284
00:17:14,680 --> 00:17:15,777
Dash wouldn't do that!

285
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:17,566
He isn't that kind of person!

286
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:22,100
Come to think of it...

287
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:30,760
So you won't kill no matter what, huh?

288
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,297
You are disgusting!

289
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:35,557
You know what, Vast?

290
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:37,758
You're nothing but a damn hypocrite!

291
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:43,388
There's no way you haven't had to kill
troublemakers somewhere along the line!

292
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:45,100
How do I know?

293
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:49,869
Because nobody can survive what you've
been through without hurting somebody!

294
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:54,019
The sixty billion double dollar
bounty on your head is proof of that!

295
00:17:56,720 --> 00:18:00,400
Well, what do you have to say
for yourself, Vasta Stampede?

296
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:04,000
Why won't he say anything?

297
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:07,974
Why is he just standing there
taking that kind of abuse?

298
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,250
Hm.

299
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,710
Hm?

300
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,694
You're finally ready to fight, are you?

301
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:29,180
Oh, so you want to draw.

302
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:32,877
It's pointless no matter
what caliber pistol you use,

303
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:36,489
like trying to stop a car from
ramming at 120 miles an hour.

304
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:38,309
You felt it twice already.

305
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:42,037
Even your puny brain can realize my son's
fist is a force to be reckoned with,

306
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,717
or do you really believe
you'll survive another one?

307
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:46,780
This is your last chance to run?

308
00:18:46,980 --> 00:18:48,977
Although no matter how fast you are,

309
00:18:49,060 --> 00:18:52,766
within the next few minutes you'll
be smashed into tiny pieces.

310
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:54,620
Now pay attention,

311
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:56,577
because as a courtesy I'm going to lecture

312
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:59,317
you on just what a stupid
fool you really are.

313
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:00,700
Using this technique.

314
00:19:03,660 --> 00:19:06,320
My human mincemeat special course.

315
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:08,720
Go help them, quick.

316
00:19:09,140 --> 00:19:13,140
Enjoy being a hero for a moment,
then die in a most humiliating way.

317
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:09,660
He did it.

318
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,440
It changed course.

319
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:13,220
That was great.

320
00:20:16,140 --> 00:20:21,360
He caused my son's fist to be off course
with six little bullets. Not quite, Doc.

321
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:27,220
I have one left, could be my special one.

322
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:38,860
My baby!

323
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:49,777
That was terrible!

324
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:51,177
I can't believe it!

325
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:52,377
Did you see what he did?

326
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,660
He really beat him!

327
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,817
And he did it with only six bullets!

328
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:56,730
Unbelievable!

329
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:04,440
Suddenly it's become very clear to me
why he is called the Humanoid Typhoon.

330
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:07,637
It's actually him.

331
00:21:07,720 --> 00:21:08,740
He's for real.

332
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,240
The legendary outlaw.

333
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,837
Bash the Stampede!

334
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,120
You're amazing!

335
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:20,740
That's nice of you guys to say that,
but I'm no more amazing than you are.

336
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,700
It ain't over yet!

337
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:26,980
What? What the?

338
00:21:27,940 --> 00:21:29,999
That's twice you've saved me today.

339
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:31,350
Hey!

340
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,180
Don't ignore me, you!

341
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:38,260
Don't think you won, even for a second.

342
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,677
Let's call it quits already.

343
00:21:39,760 --> 00:21:46,260
After all now, this land is
made of love and peace! Huh?

344
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:58,200
Love and peace!

345
00:21:58,980 --> 00:22:00,660
What is he doing?

346
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:03,317
Come on now, you gotta
write the company reports!

347
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:04,230
Hurry up!

348
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:06,417
Love and peace!

349
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:08,700
M .Stryfe Company report,

350
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:13,497
four months and 12 days after receiving
our orders for the insurance investigation,

351
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:18,580
we achieved contact with our
target, the man called Vash.

352
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:24,057
Contact with our target, the
man simply known as Vash the...

353
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:25,960
Love and Peace!

354
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:28,680
No, make it go away!

355
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:30,120
I can't stand anymore!

356
00:22:30,460 --> 00:22:32,360
Now everybody, join along!

357
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:34,280
Love and Peace!

358
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,800
Let's go.

359
00:23:41,980 --> 00:23:46,397
I'll see you

360
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:50,100
next time.

361
00:24:06,840 --> 00:24:12,060
The longer one holds onto a memory,
the longer one lives in the past.

362
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:18,040
The deeper the memory they hold onto,
the more beautiful the past will become.

363
00:24:19,220 --> 00:24:22,396
The beautiful memories will
eventually turn into hate.

364
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:26,195
Even if they look ahead, they
lose the ability to walk.

365
00:24:26,940 --> 00:24:30,977
As long as the heavy chain called
revenge continues to bind the heart,

366
00:24:31,060 --> 00:24:34,660
The tears of sadness
will continue to flow.
